Z||000003||87PegasusGT||03-17-2000||01:13 PM||||Hm....Didn't I bring this up in an earlier post? Good. I'm not the only one who reached this unfortunate conclusion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But.. I went shopping for one, found a late model Rx7 Twin turbo instead. Talk aboout HOT car. It handles like a dream. I just hated to fork over $20,000 for a car with 70,000 miles on it. I KNOW my Fiero can blow it away for less than half that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sid1200||03-18-2000||04:58 AM||||87, I agree with you about the Rx7, did you get one?  I've heard the 3rd generation cars 95+ had a lot of relability problems, one thing that's not usually a problem with the MR2, at least not an abused one.  Anyways this one my cousin saw was 10k with 70k on it a 92?  what would you say decent deal for him? also considering that all prices in the SF area are higher than anywhere else esp on rice burners.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||03-18-2000||10:50 AM||||Yeah the last generation RX-7's sure did haul a$$. My old roommate had one. It was a 95 R1.  The original owner had gone through an engine, and two turbos. My roommate, Scott, who now races for Porsche, bought the car with 24,000 miles on it. After a month of driving it, the RX-7 was in the shop permanently. It just wouldn't run right. The shop ended up replacing the engine again, and two more turbos. As soon as he got it back, it was traded in on a 4-Runner! I guess the original owner didn't know about Rotary engines, and how they can't be turned off cold, you've got to give the engine time to warm up!<P>As for the MR2's, I don't like them, IMHO<BR>I drove an 87 a long time ago, before my Fiero obsession, and I wasn't impressed. Looked cool, but was slow! The newer MR2 look a little better, but they don't do anything for me. Around here, I don't see too many riced up MR2's, nothing but those Eclipses and Civics (ha ha), I only see women driving the MR2 turbos.  ||||reg||13
Z||000006||87PegasusGT||03-23-2000||03:41 PM||||Reliability was part of why I didn't buy the RX7. That and the fact that I would be forking over $1000 every month (includes insurance) just to drive it. I wouldn't have any $ left for my Fiero.<BR>As far as MR2, the reason you don't see them riced, is because your average ricer can't afford one.(Late model turbo) The insurance premium i was quoted was actually the same as the Rx7. $497 a month.Most males just buy a Vette when they hit that. Also, most people don't know squat about them either.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||03-23-2000||04:13 PM||||87... a$497 a month insurance premium???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>what have you done to deserve that?  that is half of what I pay for my Cherokee per year.  When I get my GT running again, it will only cost me another $35/month!!  Of course, I will not be paying for colision on that car.||||reg||1
